{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966814,"nonce":"+c8nkLyoi6MVRXNnwO6+4EQ1084=","title":"Current state of Blinc's layout-tree stability layer. Three pieces shipped — LayoutNodeId","message":"Captures what the \"layout tree stability\" work actually became after `project-stable-node-id-design` landed and evolved. That earlier note describes the initial identity-mapping refactor; the system that exists now is broader and what matters for downstream design.\n\n**Why:** Future architectural moves (implicit signal-bound modifiers, per-property reactivity, compositor fast-path extensions) need to know which IDs survive what kind of update, and where the patch channels are. Re-deriving this from the codebase every time is wasteful and error-prone — I conflated `StableNodeId` with the broader stability layer in 2026-05-24 and proposed work that's already half-shipped.\n\n**How to apply:** When asked \"what survives a rebuild\" or \"where do we patch a single property,\" consult this. When designing a reactive primitive, default to wiring through `queue_prop_update` (the closure form, see below) before reaching for `Stateful` rebuild.\n\n\n`RenderTree::incremental_update(element)` ([renderer/build/entry.rs:128](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/entry.rs#L128)) is the canonical update entry. It hashes the new element tree via `DivHash::compute_element_tree`, classifies the diff in `analyze_changes` ([build/diff.rs](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/diff.rs)) as `ChangeCategory { layout, visual, children, handlers }`, and dispatches:\n- `VisualOnly` / `LayoutChanged` → `update_render_props_in_place` ([build/diff.rs:221](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/diff.rs#L221)). Patches `RenderProps` and (if `layout`) the taffy `Style`. **LayoutNodeId unchanged in the slotmap.**\n- `ChildrenChanged` → `rebuild_children_in_place` ([build/diff.rs:40](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/build/diff.rs#L40)). Scoped wipe + recollect under the affected parent. Sibling subtrees keep their LayoutNodeIds.\n\nSo a Stateful closure re-run that only flips `.bg(red) → .bg(blue)` lands as `VisualOnly`, the slotmap key for that node is preserved, and the patch is `RenderProps[same_layout_id].bg = blue`.\n\nFor the structural-rebuild case (and for state attached to nodes that need to survive a slotmap key change), `StableNodeId(u64)` is derived from `(parent_stable ⊕ sibling_index, optional element_id)` via `derive_child` in [tree.rs:66](crates/blinc_layout/src/tree.rs#L66). Two-way maps on `RenderTree`: `stable_to_layout`, `layout_to_stable` ([renderer/mod.rs:765](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/mod.rs#L765)).\n\nConsumers already migrated:\n- `HandlerRegistry` (event_handler.rs)\n- `CssAnimationStore` (render_state.rs)\n- Motion bindings + layout animations (auto stable_key — commits `2a5b8a32`, `bac96fd4`)\n- Hooks `use_state` / `use_signal` auto-key via `#[track_caller]` (commits `37c79fcf`, `bf44e80d`)\n- `EventRouter.pressed_target` (gotcha-event-router-layout-id-staleness)\n\n- [stateful.rs:789](crates/blinc_layout/src/stateful.rs#L789) `queue_prop_update(node_id, props)` — pushes full-RenderProps replace onto a process-global queue and calls `request_redraw()`.\n- [stateful.rs:778](crates/blinc_layout/src/stateful.rs#L778) `take_pending_prop_updates()` — drained by windowed.rs (~5071) every frame; each entry applied via `RenderTree::update_render_props` ([renderer/mod.rs:2236](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/mod.rs#L2236)).\n- `RenderTree::update_render_props(node_id, |p| ...)` is a closure-form mutator — already supports partial updates.\n- Compositor fast path: `apply_binding_deltas` ([renderer/paint/motion.rs](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/paint/motion.rs)) and `apply_css_deltas` patch cached batches in place after the queue is drained. Cache invalidate tag: `\"stateful_prop_update\"`.\n\n\nThe infrastructure is ~95% there. Missing pieces:\n\n1. **`IntoReactive\u003cT\u003e` trait** dispatched on every Div builder method so `.bg(red)` (eager) and `.bg(\u0026state)` (bound) share the same call-site shape.\n2. **`PropertyBindingRegistry` on RenderTree**: `HashMap\u003cSignalId, Vec\u003c(LayoutNodeId, FieldWriter)\u003e\u003e`. Populated in `Div::build` / `collect_render_props` when a binding is detected.\n3. **`queue_prop_update_partial(node_id, FnOnce(\u0026mut RenderProps))`** — closure form, parallel to existing full-replace `queue_prop_update`. The drain in windowed.rs picks it up and applies via `update_render_props`.\n4. **`State\u003cT\u003e::set` hook**: after writing the cell, walk `registry[signal_id]`, for each `(layout_id, writer)` call `queue_prop_update_partial(layout_id, |p| writer(p, \u0026new_value))`.\n5. **Cleanup**: `remove_subtree_nodes` drops registry entries for removed LayoutNodeIds. `Div::build` running on a node with existing bindings overwrites the registry entries (correct by construction — the new builder re-reads the signal for initial value AND re-registers).\n\nThe registry can key directly on `LayoutNodeId` (not StableNodeId) because `Div::build` is the only thing that registers entries, and `Div::build` runs in exactly the situations where LayoutNodeId might have just been regenerated. So the registry is naturally coherent with the slotmap state.\n\nFor structurally surviving subtrees (the common case), the LayoutNodeId is stable per Layer 1, the registry entry is stable, signal.set patches the same node every time.\n\n**Don't re-propose this as if it were greenfield work.** Most of the supporting code already exists; the new bits are concentrated in `IntoReactive`, the partial-form queue API, and the registry + setter hook.\n\n\n- Identity layer history: [[project-stable-node-id-design]] (older, design-time)\n- Cost analysis vs. Vizia: [[project-blinc-perf-vs-vizia]] — the `.bg(signal)` patch pattern is exactly what Vizia's `modifier!` does at `modifiers/mod.rs:50`\n- Latent gotchas in the patch path: [[gotcha-fast-path-visible-anim-latch]], [[gotcha-spinner-pinned-text-collect]], [[gotcha-canvas-fast-path-freeze]]","files":null}]}